(/--- StaffSync Full Stack Project Documentation (Page 1 of 6) ---) '
() '
(# StaffSync HRMS   Comprehensive Project Documentation) '
() '
(## 1. System Overview) '
(**StaffSync** is an enterprise Human Resource Management System engineered to streaml) '
(  ine workforce operations, time and attendance, multi-tiered leave approvals, employ) '
(  ee learning, organizational announcements, and compliance auditing.) '
() '
(The system is architected as a modular full-stack application featuring a React 19 si) '
(  ngle-page application frontend and an Express REST API backend, supported by a dual) '
(  -engine storage architecture \(MongoDB Atlas with automatic in-memory fallback\).) '
() '
(---) '
() '
(## 2. Technology Stack) '
() '
(| Layer | Technologies & Libraries |) '
(| :--- | :--- |) '
(| **Frontend Framework** | React 19 \(`react`, `react-dom`\), TypeScript 5.8+ |) '
(| **Styling & Design System** | Tailwind CSS v4 \(`@tailwindcss/vite`\), Lucide Icons \() '
(  `lucide-react`\) |) '
(| **Build & Tooling** | Vite 6, `tsx` Node TypeScript runtime, ESLint |) '
(| **Backend Runtime** | Node.js, Express 4.x, HTTP/REST |) '
(| **Database & ORM** | MongoDB Atlas, Mongoose 8.x, In-Memory MemoryStore Fallback |) '
(| **Security & Auth** | JSON Web Tokens \(`jsonwebtoken`\), `bcryptjs`, CORS middleware) '
(   |) '
(| **Charts & Data Viz** | Recharts 2.x, Custom SVG Data Metric Cards |) '
(| **Data Export** | Structured CSV Generator \(UTF-8 formatted\) |) '
() '
(---) '
() '
(## 3. Project Directory Structure) '
() '
(StaffSync is organized into distinct layers for frontend client assets, server busine) '
(  ss logic, and modular packages:) '
() '
(```) '
(/) '
(    staffsync/                         # Modular Project Root) '
(        client/                        # Frontend Application \(Client\)) '
(            api/                       # API HTTP client & service wrappers) '
(                client.ts              # Axios/Fetch client with JWT interceptor) '
(            components/                # Reusable UI components) '
ET
endstream
